  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two long straight parallel wires, carrying (adjustable) currents <math><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> , are kept at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math>&nbsp;apart. If the force <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math>&nbsp;between the two wires is taken as &#39;positive&#39; when the wires repel each other and &#39;negative&#39; when the wires attract each other, the graph showing the dependence of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math>, on the product <math><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> , would be:</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
